A||||13||theogre||It's Official.... STF Vs. 5W-30 in Isuzu 5 speed||||10||
Z||000000||theogre||12-30-2001||01:56 PM||||I was digging thru TSB's looking for something else when I found this one.... (I'll add this to the cave next week.)<P>88-7-31 5/88<BR>Transmission Fluid Usage (Cold Weather Shiftability)<P>Affected, All 1983-88 Sunbird, Grand Am, and Fiero with <u>Isuzu</u> 5 speed<P>Summary, Paraphrased.....<BR>Some people are complaining of gear clash and/or stiff shifter in cold weather.<P>Fix:<P>Drian the tranny and refil with Synchromesh Transmission Fluid. (PN 12345349)<P>Refilling with 5W-30 is ok, but it will not provide the lower shift effort that the STF provides. The most noticable reduction in effort will be during cold weather operation.<P>Mixing STF with 5W-30 is ok but the more 5W-30 present, the stiffer the tranny will be, especially cold.<P>(Direct Qutoe)<BR>NOTICE: DO NOT USE ANY AMOUNT OF ATF (AUTOMATIC TRANSMISSION FLUID) IN ANY MODEL YEAR. THE USE OF ATF MAY CAUSE GEAR CLASH AND RESULT IN SYNCHRONIZER DAMAGE.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000001||mrfixit58||12-30-2001||05:36 PM||||Ogre,<P>Just to let you know that I followed up on your advise and changed to the GM Synchromesh fluid in my 88 GT 5-speed and I could really tell the difference. The movement from 1st to 2nd and from 3rd to 4th is sooooo smooth. I still have a detent (sp?) cable problem but will get to that soon.<P>Again, thanks for the advise,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||14
Z||000002||Formula88||12-30-2001||05:58 PM||||Same here.  I just put GM Synchromesh in my Getrag (88 Formula) and the difference between it and 5W30 motor oil is night and day!  I'll use nothing less in my Fiero from now on.  It's WORTH the $10 per quart!||||reg||14
Z||000003||Joe Torma||12-30-2001||06:25 PM||||I guess as soon as I fix my leak I should switch my 4sp's oil.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||12-30-2001||06:25 PM||||The only stuff I use is better than synchromesh fluid, It is made by<BR>redline. It is called MTL. It gives a huge difference in shifter feel and<BR>protects the trans. & syncros better than most anything on the market. It is<BR>purple oil. Look at it at <A HREF="http://www.redlineoil.com/products.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.redlineoil.com/products.htm</A> <P><BR>I use it in my Isuzu and my getrag. They feel better than new. both have<BR>160,000 miles or more on them too<P><BR>You can do a search online to find a place that sells it. For best feel and<BR>protection for your trans. I would recommend it.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||12-31-2001||12:14 AM||||I'm just collecting all the "official stuff" from GM on the subject. Trying to end all the confusion over what's in various books...<P>In other threads, some people like redline and others have said they like STF better. It doesn't matter to me. I have an automatic. Either way the link to that is in the existing stick article in my cave... ||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||12-31-2001||12:51 AM||||I'm actually a very recent Redline MTL -&gt; Syncromesh convert!<P>Finally got around to trying the GM fluid itself, and it's better.  The redline was good, the Syncromesh is AWESOME.<P>Turns out our cars have funky composite syncros that need the special GM Mojo.  The "syncromesh' is also a Synthetic fluid, so hey.<P>Just don't know what to do with the case of MTL I have sitting in my garage, doh!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88CoupeV6:<BR><B>The only stuff I use is better than synchromesh fluid, It is made by<BR>redline. It is called MTL. It gives a huge difference in shifter feel and<BR>protects the trans. & syncros better than most anything on the market. It is<BR>purple oil. Look at it at <A HREF="http://www.redlineoil.com/products.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.redlineoil.com/products.htm</A> <P><BR>I use it in my Isuzu and my getrag. They feel better than new. both have<BR>160,000 miles or more on them too<P><BR>You can do a search online to find a place that sells it. For best feel and<BR>protection for your trans. I would recommend it.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||Formula88||12-31-2001||08:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>Just don't know what to do with the case of MTL I have sitting in my garage, doh!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sell it to 88CoupeV6!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||3
Z||000008||Eriamjh||12-31-2001||09:41 AM||||I've been running synthetic 5W-30 in mine with no troubles for 4 years.  155K miles.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dumba$$||12-31-2001||11:13 AM||||i just bought some of the syncromesch grom GM the other day ,it will be going in my 4.10 when it gets put in tomorrow,<BR>i figure, if your gonna do it mise well do it right!!<BR>my cost, whell Fierogods cost on it was 7.10/qt.<BR>im sure it will be worth the extra$$$<P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>ever notice that people that own a fiero, either have, or have had other fieros?||||reg||1
Z||000010||tesmith66||12-31-2001||11:30 AM||||Ben,<P>Put it up for sale on the Probe Talk forum. Those 93-97 Ford Probe GT MTX guys are nuts for the Redline stuff.<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000011||StuGood||12-31-2001||04:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>Finally got around to trying the GM fluid itself, and it's better.  The redline was good, the Syncromesh is AWESOME...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>FWIW, your testimony carries considerable weight with me.  I remember you posting earlier how much you liked the Redline stuff.  Now you've tried both, and if the difference is that dramatic, there's obviously something to it.<P>After that, the only things that remain in question are long-term effects (i.e.- wear, durability), and Ogre's research settles that matter as far as I am concerned.<P>Thanks, guys.  That's what I like about this Forum - honest data, mostly free of B.S.   (that's - Bombastic Statements, of course  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). ||||reg||14
Z||000012||Formula88||12-31-2001||05:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eriamjh:<BR><B>I've been running synthetic 5W-30 in mine with no troubles for 4 years.  155K miles.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh, I'd been running 5W-30 in my car as long as I've had it.  LZeitgeist had done the same in his 88 Coupe with over 250,000 miles and his 60,000 mile original Formula.  No problems.  But when we switched to Synchromesh, the transmission shifts VERY much smoother.  It's only about $20 for 2 quarts.  That's all you need.  Trust me, you won't be disappointed.  You'll notice the difference immediately.||||reg||14
Z||000013||artherd||12-31-2001||07:55 PM||||Heh, we're not even afraid to eat out own words! (most of the time :P)<P>Yeah, the Redline did work, and it beat engine oil hands down, and it was all cool and RED and raceing and synthetic and awesome!  <BR>But with the Syncromesh it's like there' an extra hand PULLING the shifter into gear for you!  <P>Shifts are measurably *quicker* as well, even  (and espeically) when you're really driving the car.  It *really* loves rooling through the gears between 4grand and 5500 now!<P>The feel now is most remenicent of the first Ferrari I ever drove, a 91 Mondial Cabriolet 3.2.  Felt like the sprit of Enzo himself was in the passanger seat guiding my hands over the shifter!  Man, that car felt great at speed!<P><BR>PS: I needed nearly 3 quarts (about 2.75 used) to get my 88 Getrag full.  I don't think 2 will be enough, hasn't been on either of my cars with any tranny fluid.<P>Long and short? After trying them all, I'll be using Syncromesh in both my stock 2.8 T-top car, and my ~365bhp Northstar car! (both getrags.)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by StuGood:<BR><B>FWIW, your testimony carries considerable weight with me.  I remember you posting earlier how much you liked the Redline stuff.  <BR>Thanks, guys.  That's what I like about this Forum - honest data, mostly free of B.S.   (that's - Bombastic Statements, of course   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ). </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
